A||N||22||anthony_86gt||Should I Brag???||||5||
Z||000000||anthony_86gt||07-28-2001||11:34 PM||||Alright guys here is the deal.  I am 16 years old and I have a 86 1/2 GT with a 5 speed manual.  My friend just got a 98 Mustang.  His Mustand is just the standard model with the v-6 and it is automatic.  I was wondering if i should brag or not.  Who would win in a 1/4 race.  We are going to go to the drag strip around here and see.  But let me know what you guys think.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rogue_Ant||07-28-2001||11:38 PM||||Are you good at driving a stick?  If it was me I would brag, V-6 mustangs aren't very fast.  Would powershift 1-2 & 2-3 and leave him looking at your tailights.<P>Rogue||||reg||6
Z||000002||anthony_86gt||07-28-2001||11:49 PM||||Yeah i am good with a stick, but what do you mean by power shifting?  I will brag my a$$ now.  Thanks, but if there is any good tips let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||12:05 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by anthony_86gt:<BR><B>Yeah i am good with a stick, but what do you mean by power shifting?  I will brag my a$$ now.  Thanks, but if there is any good tips let me know.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Power shifting is when you shift without letting your foot off of the floor.  I wouldn't do it much, but its good a couple of tens.  Otherwise do basic things that you can, like plugs, wires, cap & rotor, K&N filter.  Also remove the water seperator from your intake if you haven't already, here is a link if you don't know how:<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.floridafieros.org/osg/mod.intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.floridafieros.org/osg/mod.intake.html</A> <P>Rogue<P><p>[This message has been edited by Rogue_Ant (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||12:22 AM||||Oh as a side-note I found this little info:<P>Myth: The Fiero was not a quick car<P>Fact: The V6 Fiero accelerated from 0-30 in 2.2 seconds. Thats the same as the Lamborghini Diablo.<P>Myth: The Fiero was a slow car.<P>Fact: The best 1/4- mile time for a stock V6 Fiero is 14.7 @ 92 mph. Thats faster than the stock automatic 5.0L Mustang<P>Myth: The Fiero was not a high speed car.<P>Fact: The best top speed for a stock V6 Fiero was 135mph. Thats the same as the 85-93 Ford Mustang.<P>I also looked up the 3.8 Auto Mustang for you and found a guy posting a high 16's timeslip.<P>Rogue||||reg||12
Z||000005||Black88GT||07-29-2001||12:35 AM||||Rogue, no stock V6 Fiero runs 14.7s.||||reg||1
Z||000006||anthony_86gt||07-29-2001||12:35 AM||||Thanks rogue!  I read that somewhere too, and now i just remembered it!  I can't wait until he gets back from vacation. I will let you know what happens.||||reg||7
Z||000007||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||01:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Rogue, no stock V6 Fiero runs 14.7s.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah you have a point, was just cut & pasting from WS6's web site.<P>But here is a quote from banditbalz:<P>15.2 at 90 mp/h <BR>no cat, no NOS, no B.S.<P>stock 4 speed muncie, stock 2.8 <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A>  <BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<P>So maybe that is closer, but it is still better then a second faster in the 1/4 then an auto 3.8 mustang<P><BR>Rogue||||reg||1
Z||000008||banditbalz||07-29-2001||10:07 AM||||Just to let you guys know, I power shifted both 1-2 and 2-3 to acheive that time. Be careful doing this in an '88 (no rev limiter). <BR>_<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HardLaunch_3.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Frank Sombers||07-29-2001||10:35 AM||||Brag if you like, but do it at Fiero Chat..NOT HERE.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Will||07-29-2001||01:44 PM||||I think you should win <I>before</I> you put your foot in your mouth.<BR>Further, I think that you should be a gracious winner, which is harder than being a sportsman after a loss.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||07-29-2001||02:41 PM||||As for top speed, no magazine, save for Auto Week (8/10/87) could get a Fiero over 128 mph for top speed, broke 130 mph. (Unless you count the SD-4 Fiero from Car and Driver that reached 131 mph or the full race GTU Fiero at 161 mph and that was an 88 Formula. The 14.7 second 1/4 mile (at 93 mph)that you quoted was from a Super Duty Fiero tested by Car and Driver (6/85). The quickest 1/4 time was from Car and Driver who got their 86 GT down to 15.9 seconds @ 85 mph. However, Road & Track got their 88 Formula up to 85.5 in 16 flat.<P>Never brag your ass off. There only a few things more childish than bragging before you even win a race. Let your car do the talking and just smile. Don't underestimate the power of a 3.8. That liter displacement advantage plus the more efficient, modern intake engineering might be quicker than you think.<P>Source: "Fiero" by Gary Witzenburg. Love this book!||||reg||6
Z||000012||hyhy4u||07-29-2001||05:22 PM||||I raced my bro in laws 95 Mustang..last year they made the 5.0 V8, and i kicked his butt!!..hes got a 5 speed in it to!!, After that hes never made fun of my car again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||beachbomb||07-29-2001||09:24 PM||||HI, if you have my kind of luck, NEVER brag, i've bragged twice about my car(first time i bragged i got a small electrical fire, second time the timing gear went out on it) i will NEVER again brag about my car....good luck..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||10
Z||000014||artherd||07-29-2001||11:51 PM||||If you can drive, your Fiero will be a faster car than the mustang you describe.<P>The v6 stickshift cars are also slower than a properly running v6 fiero.<P>As another said, the fiero is *blindingly* quick to 30mph or so, thank the mid-engine weight transfers!  Now if it only had ~220bhp from the factory... (TDC 3.4 :)<P>Bragging is just another way of overcompensating for a lack of something else... :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000015||Capt Fiero||07-30-2001||12:13 AM||||Just be carefull you must take 2 things into account, first off a NEW Fiero can do mid to high 15's Motortrend said it was 16.1 and Hot Rod claimed 15.8, now is your motor brand new or as good as new, and the mustang how new is it, when you look at book facts there can be one set of book numbers and a totally diffent result at the strip (or stoplight) your best bet is to just say you want to race for the fun of it.  I raced this guy in an 5.0 Mustange and beat him over and over again, then the next weekend he came out and wanted to race again, and I got slaughterd, with bolt ons his stang went from 14.9 down to 13.6.   My point is driver + car + motor hell even wheels and tires, can make a huge diff. Race for fun not bragging rights !! <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415">  <p>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroMontreal||07-30-2001||12:27 AM||||Hey David, are you trying to show us that your car is Burning Oil?<P>J/K||||reg||1
Z||000017||Smoooooth GT||07-30-2001||12:55 AM||||oh noooo ....  not another fire....lol  <BR>good burn...                <P>------------------<BR>NEW EMAIL..  Smooth_gt@k.st<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">     <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||1
Z||000018||DKOV||07-30-2001||01:48 AM||||I'm confused...  I might buy that 0-60 thing but the top speed ONLY 135mph?<P>When I took my Fiero (back when it was a 2.8) to the track for "race school" the first time, my instructor told me that 140 was fast enough and not to try THAT again!  Of course, one wheel was a bit (a LOT) out of balance so the car danced around a bit at that speed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, all that was modified on that motor was K&N and a Super Chip.<P>So what gives?  I can't possibly be the only person ont he planet that has had their fiero above 140... Can I?<P>Please, nobody flame me or think that I am lying just to start an argument.  I am willing to believe that if it is NOT possible, then I must have seen wrong or the speedo was out of psync or something but...<P>It sure FELT like 140+...<P>Anyway, the track time was relatively short lived.  I blew the front Driver's strut under breaking for a double apex right.  Let me tell you what... A couple of 360s at around 100mph will wake you up in a HURRY!<P>Any of you that run at PIR have probably heard the story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, I think the Fiero is everything it was cracked up to be... and MORE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000019||My7Fieros||07-30-2001||01:53 AM||||Ive got a brand new 2001 Mustang V6...and I (obviously) have Fieros to, (all 6 cylenders), auto, 4 speed, and 5 speed. I LOVE my Mustang, but any one of my Fieros will run circles around it, <B>PERIOD</B>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Capt Fiero||07-30-2001||11:54 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Smoooooth GT:<BR><B>oh noooo ....  not another fire....lol  <BR>good burn...                <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actully the pic does not come out right, I need to resize it a bit, in the full size pic it shows that both tires are spinning ( 2 perfect black marks left on the pavment just behind the car)  Most people think that I have a V8 or something, but it is just my mildly built V6. But thanks for the comment.<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>   <p>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
